{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book","id":1130339,"title":"Contagion Chronicle book","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-17T10:18:40-07:00","id":1130339,"title":"Contagion Chronicle book","content":"From 2017 Onyx Path brochure:<br /> <br /> <i>'The <b>Contagion Chronicle</b> is an overarching Chronicle consisting of chronicle hooks, riveting settings, and Storyteller aids to help present all the <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> game lines into one consistent story. In the chronicle, the Contagion acts as a motivational force and inspires the formation of factions where vampires, werewolves, mages, mummies, etc. come together in new and unique ways.<br /> <br /> Once joined together to deal with the Contagion, these factions will never see their world (or each other) the same way, and will be forever changed. Each time the Contagion emerges to threaten the fabric of our world, the only beings capable of manipulating, slowing, weaponizing, or halting it, are the unnatural denizens from across the <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>. The Contagion permeates Infrastructure and warps the known antagonists and supporting blocks present in the lives of every inhuman being.'</i><br /> <br /> Year ago it was announced as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle\">C</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle\">rossover Chronicle</a>. I started this new topic as previous have over 25 pages and in this one I wanted to focus on the Contagion ideas and inspirations for the main Chronicle idea in the book.<br /> <br /> <b>How would you see supernaturals societies responses to Contagion?</b> Creation of new superfactions based on Covenants, Tribes, Orders, etc.? Break of any previous factions? World scale scenarios?<br /> <br /> On first throw I would add whole <b>Secret World</b> franchise - in this MMO cRPG you fight with some supernatural super mystical alien disease called <i>Filth</i>. Probably Contagion works more or less the same in CoD universe. Just see ( or play, game is now free ) yourself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z3DWhG6K7j4\" data-code=\"z3DWhG6K7j4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/z3DWhG6K7j4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-17-2017, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:06:08-07:00","id":1130389,"title":"","content":"I'm somewhat excited for it; I'm excited for some answers about questions, and hopefully some advice for storytellers on how to run a Chronicle that uses multiple splats. My few experiences with Crossover have been somewhat fun, but a little hard to wrap my head around; as a ST and player alike I'd like to see some advice for that.<br /> <br /> Though using one big overarching theme to connect the splats really helps alot, not gonna lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:08:59-07:00","id":1130424,"title":"","content":"Is this related to the crossover chronicle? brochure didn't specified. If so, eh, was expecting another approach. But I guess that's the only reason to mix games. Huge fucking threat which makes them band together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:14:30-07:00","id":1130431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130424#post1130424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this related to the crossover chronicle? brochure didn't specified.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brochure did not mention any other gamelines crossover related Chronicle book, so I assume it's the same book as previous Crossover Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:14:43-07:00","id":1130432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130424#post1130424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this related to the crossover chronicle? brochure didn't specified. If so, eh, was expecting another approach. But I guess that's the only reason to mix games. Huge fucking threat which makes them band together.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I can tell, this <i>is</i> the Crossover Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:55:01-07:00","id":1130460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130432#post1130432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I can tell, this <i>is</i> the Crossover Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do believe you are right. It has the same graphic in the brochure as the Crossover Chronicle did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:03:04-07:00","id":1130466,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how I feel about the Contagion thing, partly because I don't know what to expect from it and partly because I was hoping this book would primarily be mechanical and thematic advice for blending the lines. Pinning the book on an external threat makes me worry a little bit about how much actual crossover we'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:45:19-07:00","id":1130498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130466#post1130466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how I feel about the Contagion thing, partly because I don't know what to expect from it and partly because I was hoping this book would primarily be mechanical and thematic advice for blending the lines. Pinning the book on an external threat makes me worry a little bit about how much actual crossover we'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I get where you're coming from. I felt a little irrelevant in one Chronicle I played because I was playing an Invictus Ventrue with an Elodoth and a Mastigos sliver ladder. I often felt like I was trying to play catch up with the other characters; oh well, I'm certain we'll get some mechanical advice or answers in this book. <br /> <br /> Like what happens when vampires diablerize other splats (vampires are capable of diablerizing vampires and mortals alike, so I figure this might be a question that should be asked).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:55:39-07:00","id":1130510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130466#post1130466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how I feel about the Contagion thing, partly because I don't know what to expect from it and partly because I was hoping this book would primarily be mechanical and thematic advice for blending the lines. Pinning the book on an external threat makes me worry a little bit about how much actual crossover we'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I'm wondering that as well.<br /> <br /> Taking the name at face value, having Contagion JUST be a supernatural disease is...incredibly underwhelming. Next guess would be some kind of organization but having an antagonist organization that somehow draws the ire of every single supernatural creature in CofD is...a little too special snowflake-y.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:01:08-07:00","id":1130518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130498#post1130498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I get where you're coming from. I felt a little irrelevant in one Chronicle I played because I was playing an Invictus Ventrue with an Elodoth and a Mastigos sliver ladder. I often felt like I was trying to play catch up with the other characters; oh well, I'm certain we'll get some mechanical advice or answers in this book.<br /> <br /> Like what happens when vampires diablerize other splats (vampires are capable of diablerizing vampires and mortals alike, so I figure this might be a question that should be asked).</div> </div> </div> </div>My hopes for this book are mostly stuff like <i>The Lost and the Unchained both wear masks and are on the run; here's where you can overlap that in a chronicle and here's interesting points where they contrast</i> or <i>In a story with Prometheans and Mummies, an easy heart for that is juxtaposing those climbing towards humanity with those who've lost it</i> with a little bit of <i>Hey, here's a Lodge that focuses on the Astral </i>or <i>We've updated this Bloodline and refocused it on Memory now that the Fog of Ages is gone</i>, but I feel like that's not what I'm gonna get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:29:32-07:00","id":1130538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130510#post1130510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I'm wondering that as well.<br /> <br /> Taking the name at face value, having Contagion JUST be a supernatural disease is...incredibly underwhelming. Next guess would be some kind of organization but having an antagonist organization that somehow draws the ire of every single supernatural creature in CofD is...a little too special snowflake-y.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wonder if there is a connection to the Infected minor template in Hurt Locker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:45:49-07:00","id":1130551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130538#post1130538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if there is a connection to the Infected minor template in Hurt Locker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, isn't it? I'm really hoping there is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:23:21-07:00","id":1130571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130551#post1130551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, isn't it? I'm really hoping there is.</div> </div> </div> </div> It'd be odd if it didn't, a teaser for Contagion Chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T18:37:50-07:00","id":1130637,"title":"","content":"Anyone reminded of IDW's Infestation? Sure hope that this isn't just every splat getting some sort of mindless/hive mind apocalypse-class enemy.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, my other big concern is how they plan on making any splat other than Mages and Mummies relevant. I say this as someone whose fav splat is Changelings. I guess you could go the Hunter route, but ...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T18:43:00-07:00","id":1130639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130637#post1130637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, my other big concern is how they plan on making any splat other than Mages and Mummies relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would Mages and Mummies be relevant?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T18:49:40-07:00","id":1130641,"title":"","content":"Theyre the most out and out powerful splats right? I know power's not everything, but unless they're really holding the Idiot Ball, they're gonna be both the big guns and the specialist agents against whatever this contagion turns out to be.<br /> <br /> Plus, haven't people been grumbling for years that the difference in both subtle and overt power levels between some splats made crossover really hard? This could fix that if they do it well","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T18:57:00-07:00","id":1130646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130641#post1130641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theyre the most out and out powerful splats right? I know power's not everything, but unless they're really holding the Idiot Ball, they're gonna be both the big guns and the specialist agents against whatever this contagion turns out to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you know comics, you might look more at the Blackest Night than Infestation, where people have to work together to solve the problem. This doesn't seem like the kind of situation where a mage can just Life 4 it away, or a werewolf or vampire can just ignore it, for one reason or another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, haven't people been grumbling for years that the difference in both subtle and overt power levels between some splats made crossover really hard? This could fix that if they do it well </div> </div> </div>It says it's going to 'warp the...supporting blocks' of supernatural characters, which seems like how some of the 'balance' is going to be done. Though the problem with crossover is more with thematics than power, as that can just be overcome with Experience. The story context has always been the big thing. If you have a crossover group, you generally have most characters completely separate from the supernatural setting of their gameline, in favor of one other characters setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-17-2017, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T19:27:24-07:00","id":1130651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130518#post1130518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My hopes for this book are mostly stuff like <i>The Lost and the Unchained both wear masks and are on the run; here's where you can overlap that in a chronicle and here's interesting points where they contrast</i> or <i>In a story with Prometheans and Mummies, an easy heart for that is juxtaposing those climbing towards humanity with those who've lost it</i> with a little bit of <i>Hey, here's a Lodge that focuses on the Astral </i>or <i>We've updated this Bloodline and refocused it on Memory now that the Fog of Ages is gone</i>, but I feel like that's not what I'm gonna get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah! expecting Z splat support from Onyx Path, my sweet, sweet summer child.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T19:37:48-07:00","id":1130654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130651#post1130651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hah! expecting Z splat support from Onyx Path, my sweet, sweet summer child.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an entire small book dedicated to a Z splat collection already, and there is several publically available Bloodlines on the blog itself. I am skeptical.<br /> <br /> Back to the plot: I'm hoping the Contagion is something more like the Virus from Antagonists-going full zombie apocalypse is its &quot;panic&quot; condition, it prefers to live as asymptomatic carriers and spread as far as possible.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'm hoping that the Contagion is the new name for the Virus-it fits better, and its very biology (a living meme that feeds on urban legends) makes it a natural rival and uneasy ally for...everyone (want someone scared or lore to be made more public? The Contagion's got you covered. Want to remain secret or to keep everyone calm? The Contagion is your worst nightmare).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T19:59:41-07:00","id":1130665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130654#post1130654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is an entire small book dedicated to a Z splat collection already, and there is several publically available Bloodlines on the blog itself. I am skeptical.<br /> <br /> Back to the plot: I'm hoping the Contagion is something more like the Virus from Antagonists-going full zombie apocalypse is its &amp;quot;panic&amp;quot; condition, it prefers to live as asymptomatic carriers and spread as far as possible.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'm hoping that the Contagion is the new name for the Virus-it fits better, and its very biology (a living meme that feeds on urban legends) makes it a natural rival and uneasy ally for...everyone (want someone scared or lore to be made more public? The Contagion's got you covered. Want to remain secret or to keep everyone calm? The Contagion is your worst nightmare).</div> </div> </div> </div>If I got my hopes up for a hard look at overlapping thematics and get a fucking zombie book I'm gonna throw myself out a window.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:04:55-07:00","id":1130668,"title":"","content":"I doubt the reasons to group up and explanations for how to do it will only be in a case of the contagion, it would be pointless in regards to crossover in general. Rose said they were providing context for crossover from the beginning. There's no reason to believe the interactions will fail past said contagion.<br /> <br /> Though it's entirely possible the Contagion itself is a zombie outbreak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:07:32-07:00","id":1130669,"title":"","content":"the brochure said the contagion chronicle kickstarter is coming in 2018. I'm hoping the writing holds off till Changeling, Geist, Hunter and mummy 2e and deviant are all into editing so that all the lines' lore &amp; rules are available for the developer's reference","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:10:31-07:00","id":1130672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130665#post1130665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I got my hopes up for a hard look at overlapping thematics and get a fucking zombie book I'm gonna throw myself out a window.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Um, I'm looking at the brochure now:<br /> <br /> The exact words are that it &quot;threatens the fabric of our world&quot; whenever it manifests. As in &quot;alters Infrastructure&quot;. In ways the players are implicitly allowed to weaponize.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's a plague that affects the <i>people</i> in it. More like what happens when <i>reality </i>gets the sniffles. It also explicitly affects existing antagonists.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, this sounds like the Abyss, but I think we may be seeing a Lower Depths incursion here (which is something that involves more gamelines, as the Strix are explicitly invaders from there).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:20:59-07:00","id":1130674,"title":"","content":"I'd expect there will be reasons from a variety of sources. Every line has things 'Contagion' can be linked to. If it was <i>just </i>a reality-shaking thing Cataclysm would make more sense.<br /> <br /> Vampire has the Plague Angel, founder of the Morbus. Werewolf has the Fire-Touched and specifically the Lodge of the Fevered Light and idigam. Mage has its Abyss. Changeling the True Fae, Prometheans lost lineages and the Centimani and on and on. You don't need to go to other worlds to find apocalypses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-17-2017, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:50:16-07:00","id":1130689,"title":"","content":"Oh boy .. the City is about get another update .. .weeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:52:55-07:00","id":1130691,"title":"","content":"It still sniffs a little too much of superhero team-up for me. I wanted organic reasons why the lines would crossover, not some brand new thing that justifies it.<br /> <br /> We'll see once the book actually exists in any meaningful form, but I'm not in love with this so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T02:19:46-07:00","id":1130750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130654#post1130654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, I'm hoping that the Contagion is the new name for the Virus-it fits better, and its very biology (a living meme that feeds on urban legends) makes it a natural rival and uneasy ally for...everyone (want someone scared or lore to be made more public? The Contagion's got you covered. Want to remain secret or to keep everyone calm? The Contagion is your worst nightmare).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man, yes, I would love if Contagion would be The Virus from <b>Antagonists</b> book! I just re-read it and it sounds ssoooo awesome to be used \u2013 it was on of those early days Horror ( or Ephemeral Beings? ) forgotten later in the whole 1E nWoD/CoD line. To ease discussion, small quote on the Virus here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u2019Antagonists, p. 130\u2019</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Background:</b> The Virus evolved alongside humanity, drawing power from cautionary tales and fables. When people talk about their fears, trying to make sense of unnatural or coping with loss, tragedy or terror, the Virus grows stronger. Like a true virus, it infects as quickly as possible, replicating itself exponentially. Unlike a virus, which kills the cells it\u2019s invades, the Virus becomes sentient as it draws power from humanity, giving it ability to reason and plan. Throughtout most of humanity history, the Virus was restricted to the small pockets of humanity; but now, with advent of mass communication, has become gigantic, intelligent entity. It knows of supernatural creatures of the world through the stories it hears through those it infected. It realized that those creatures hunt and kill humans. While Virus doesn\u2019t have any feelings for humanity that could legitimately be described as \u2018compassion\u2019 or \u2018love\u2019, it does realize that the stories that humanity trade in fear are what allows it to survive. As such, it works to expose the supernatural in a rather blunt attempt to nudge people in trading stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>He sounds very much as Abyss-changed Goetia, or something like that. Best it works to \u2018unmask\u2019 all and every supernatural monster out there. He probably even make a big hit on Integrity in general mortal population\u2026 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Other idea for Contagion could be The Hunger from the same book ( and from <b>Boston Unveiled</b> ) \u2013 but it would much more classical \u2018cannibal mutation plague\u2019. Still, it nice a cool supernatural disease. But I\u2019m all hand in for it being The Virus, it\u2019s just this awesome idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T07:58:02-07:00","id":1130818,"title":"","content":"My guess would be something similar to the core book: the front half is an examination of crossovers between each line, talking about how to blend their themes, maybe providing some mechanics that help ease the combination. And then the back half is a global crossover chronicle that can be used with any combination of games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T11:36:32-07:00","id":1130911,"title":"","content":"Soooo... Does anyone else here play Mind's Eye Society LARPs? We just finished a big crossover chronicle called Combined: the Accord. The description of this book sounds very much like it.<br /> <br /> That said, Accord was one of my favorite games to ever play in, so I am 100% in for a tabletop version!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T11:42:29-07:00","id":1130915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130911#post1130911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooo... Does anyone else here play Mind's Eye Society LARPs? We just finished a big crossover chronicle called Combined: the Accord. The description of this book sounds very much like it.<br /> <br /> That said, Accord was one of my favorite games to ever play in, so I am 100% in for a tabletop version!</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been looking to get into it. I know of a local one in my town, I've just mostly been trying to work up the courge<br /> <br /> But this Combined: The Accord sounds fun. I'll have to check it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T12:20:37-07:00","id":1130923,"title":"","content":"The description says: &quot;<i>Each time the Contagion emerges to threaten the fabric of our world, the only beings capable of manipulating, slowing, weaponizing, or halting it, are the unnatural denizens from across the <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>. The Contagion permeates Infrastructure and warps the known antagonists and supporting blocks present in the lives of every inhuman being.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> Parsing this I am thinking this means something a bit chthulhueque ie something that &quot;emerges to threaten the fabric of our world&quot;. &quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Each time&quot; suggest that it is not a permanent contagion but something that emerges periodically and taints an physical area or spiritual space from a patient zero (either an actual person or spirit or a contagion zone like radiation). <br /> <br /> &quot;Contagion permeates infrastructure and warps the known antagonists...&quot; suggests that this contagion will somehow mutate the physical and/or spiritual/supernatural nature of beings in the world that we already know shaking up the usual antagonists in a way that changes how they interact with the supernaturals against whom they usually fight or maybe drives them to fight against supernaturals they would not normally interact with. <br /> <br /> I also wonder whether this supernatural contagion will have a larger effect on the mortal world, infecting those that are close to where the contagion emerges into our world in a way that will have effects far beyond the hidden world of the supernatural. If that is the case i wonder whether it will also involve an element of breaking the veil of secrecy with mortals that is an essential part of most of the regular lines. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T13:36:03-07:00","id":1130945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130641#post1130641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theyre the most out and out powerful splats right? I know power's not everything, but unless they're really holding the Idiot Ball, they're gonna be both the big guns and the specialist agents against whatever this contagion turns out to be.<br /> <br /> Plus, haven't people been grumbling for years that the difference in both subtle and overt power levels between some splats made crossover really hard? This could fix that if they do it well</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I imagine that for crossover purposes, OPP by fiat can just make any aspect or being of the &quot;Contagion&quot; immune or resistant to supernal magic. However, I would consider such a blunt and uncreative device to force balance among the various fame lines to be lazy and theme inconsistent. <br /> <br /> In any event, I hope the majority of the books deals with actual reasons for organic crossover among the splats within the current settings, with storyteller advice and detailed crossover rules mechanics. Forcing crossover by yet another big bad external threat doesn't solve the current crossover issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T13:53:08-07:00","id":1130959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130915#post1130915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been looking to get into it. I know of a local one in my town, I've just mostly been trying to work up the courge<br /> <br /> But this Combined: The Accord sounds fun. I'll have to check it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! Join us! Sadly Accord isn't going to come back, but we are replacing it with a Crossover Space Venue inspired by the Bleeding Edge and Infinite Macabre books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T14:53:51-07:00","id":1130981,"title":"","content":"Is the Contagion the same as mentioned in Hurt Locker?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T16:37:03-07:00","id":1131008,"title":"","content":"I don't think they will only focus on the Contigan, any more the Changeling only focuses on Huntsmen, Werewolf on Idigam, Vampires on Strix, Promeathan on Firestorms, so its likely that other, aspects of crossover get Explorer too outside of, Contigan. <br /> <br /> Plus DE2 will have plenty of its own crossover material to pull from. I think DE2 and CC will dovetail well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T17:06:22-07:00","id":1131017,"title":"","content":"To be fair sounds like some crap out of Monte Cook's WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T19:43:13-07:00","id":1131085,"title":"","content":"Further news from the panel: the Contagion is infecting and warping Infrastructure and causing the fabric of reality to break down, tying into some of the old Hunter 1e material about Intersitial Terrain and that horrifying bio-mechanical alternate world from the Horror Recognition Guide. Supposedly scales all the way from personal stories to apocalyptic ones.<br /> <br /> Have to say, it's sounding less and less like the book I wanted the more I hear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 08-18-2017, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T20:56:09-07:00","id":1131111,"title":"","content":"sounds like the void is trying to reach out an touch someone<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T22:10:51-07:00","id":1131124,"title":"","content":"Infrastructure gets corrupted, fundamental aspects of each line are altered. Sounds neat.<br /> <br /> I especially like the idea that, if successful, it might get more books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T06:44:51-07:00","id":1131241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1131085#post1131085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further news from the panel: the Contagion is infecting and warping Infrastructure and causing the fabric of reality to break down, tying into some of the old Hunter 1e material about Intersitial Terrain and that horrifying bio-mechanical alternate world from the Horror Recognition Guide. Supposedly scales all the way from personal stories to apocalyptic ones.<br /> <br /> Have to say, it's sounding less and less like the book I wanted the more I hear.</div> </div> </div> </div> It actually sounds more like a shard to me then what most people were expecting when the Crossover Chronicle was announced last year. <br /> <br /> Ironically DE2 sounds more like the sort of crossover Chronicle that people were expecting then CC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T08:29:03-07:00","id":1131281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1131085#post1131085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further news from the panel: the Contagion is infecting and warping Infrastructure and causing the fabric of reality to break down, tying into some of the old Hunter 1e material about Intersitial Terrain and that horrifying bio-mechanical alternate world from the Horror Recognition Guide. Supposedly scales all the way from personal stories to apocalyptic ones.<br /> <br /> Have to say, it's sounding less and less like the book I wanted the more I hear.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, it sounds like two I thought I would never have.<br /> <br /> I've been wanting another look into that since Shadows of the UK.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T15:56:33-07:00","id":1131487,"title":"","content":"At first thought, I'm really disappointed by the tired trope of 'This horrible reality-threatening disaster will force the disparate monsters of the night to unite in order to fight it!'<br /> <br /> I was hoping for a more organic, small scale discussion of the realistic Crossovers that might happen in a universe where all of the lines exist and necessarily interact to some degree, not something so forced.<br /> <br /> That said, I honestly haven't been disappointed on the whole with any product OPP has put out, even those I had huge doubts about initially, so I'm remaining optimistic, and I'm going to try to tell myself not to judge a book by its incredibly brief synopsis years before release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T16:42:38-07:00","id":1131506,"title":"","content":"I think context is very important. It's easy enough to say 'Sure they'll work together' given some amorphous potential, but you're just going to have a book that's going to result in more questions than answers. Just like other books have done, like Chicago, with Contagion you can see how they work together in dire circumstances and, likely, in preparation for horrible events or right after them, and through that have a jumping board to extrapolate further.<br /> <br /> Sure, it would be nice if there was some sort of massive book that detailed every kind of x, y, and z-splat and how they would all act in every possible situation, but that's rather unfeasible and, even if it was done, would be too limiting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T18:04:37-07:00","id":1131535,"title":"","content":"I haven't been around the forums a lot, but I just had to stop by and express how thrilled I am about Contagion Chronicles. In fact, I was just thinking for the past month or so that CoD could really use something along the lines of ongoing campaigns that many other games seem to be adopting. It's a super useful tool for driving word of mouth and player engagement, not to mention that I just think it'd be hella fun. Hell, I found myself wanting to play the new Star Trek RPG earlier this year, even though I'm not that into Star Trek, just because it sounded cool to have my group follow an ongoing string of missions, report outcomes and just generally participate in something like that.<br /> <br /> I really hope Kickstarter gets to the point where Contagion Chronicles can become more than just a book and we end up with a neat months-long living storyline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T18:39:07-07:00","id":1131552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130945#post1130945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I imagine that for crossover purposes, OPP by fiat can just make any aspect or being of the &quot;Contagion&quot; immune or resistant to supernal magic. However, I would consider such a blunt and uncreative device to force balance among the various fame lines to be lazy and theme inconsistent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, if it goes against the supportive infrastructure, it could make regaining any kind of Supernatural Fuel harder, which would already limit mages somewhat, or make access to supernatural abilities harder (mechanically via higher costs, weaker effects, penalties etc. etc.).<br /> I would be more interested in it causing something like a power incontinence though, especially something along the lines of using supernatural powers a lot increases the risk of them going wonky. Would limit the more powerful members more strongly: a guy with a gun accidently pulling the trigger can do some damage, but replace the gun with a machine gun or a grenade gun, and you're looking at a very different type of collateral.<br /> <br /> Lazy would be something like &quot;This needs to be filled with vampire blood, so the mages down there can cast a spell on the gate only the Beast can open, but which only werewolves can find, so that the gate keeper shows up and the demons can make a deal with him to acquire the item only the changelings can use to kill the contagion&quot;. Also, cheesy.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am curious and mildly optimistic. So far, I haven't been let down by OPP, and like most if not all of the material. So yeah, let's keep it with <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1131487#post1131487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to try to tell myself not to judge a book by its incredibly brief synopsis years before release.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T19:32:15-07:00","id":1131570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dawngreeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1131535#post1131535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't been around the forums a lot, but I just had to stop by and express how thrilled I am about Contagion Chronicles. In fact, I was just thinking for the past month or so that CoD could really use something along the lines of ongoing campaigns that many other games seem to be adopting. It's a super useful tool for driving word of mouth and player engagement, not to mention that I just think it'd be hella fun. Hell, I found myself wanting to play the new Star Trek RPG earlier this year, even though I'm not that into Star Trek, just because it sounded cool to have my group follow an ongoing string of missions, report outcomes and just generally participate in something like that.<br /> <br /> I really hope Kickstarter gets to the point where Contagion Chronicles can become more than just a book and we end up with a neat months-long living storyline.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean, like, a metaplot?<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's exactly what really <i>really</i> hope doesn't happen with the Contagion Chronicle.<br /> <br /> I'm with Lex on that this sounds very different from what the initial announcement of a Crossover Chronicle had gotten me exited for. That said, it does actually sound quite cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":".  Removed unnecessary topic drift 08-19-2017, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T20:02:18-07:00","id":1131580,"title":"","content":"I'm mostly on the fence for this kind of book. I mean, I support crossover generally, and I guess an example would be useful for how to run a crossover chronicle. However, on the other hand, I really hope it doesn't set a precedent for that being the only reason these splats would work together.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I'm really interested in how his weird virus thing affects the splats themselves. The description did say something about weaponizing the contagion, so I really wanna know what that could entail. On the other hand, they could have meant that only the antagonists would or could weaponize it, so that could be a bit of a disappointment.<br /> <br /> Hopefully though, they include how the different splats typically interact beyond the contagion because a group might want to keep playing with the same characters after the main contagion drama has ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T20:03:22-07:00","id":1131581,"title":"","content":"Actually, funny thing about the Contagion Chronicle:<br /> <br /> Since DE1, I've always had the idea for a multi-generational overarching chronicle that took place across multiple Eras. Problem was, I had no idea what to have the unifying force/threat be. Didn't really want to use the God-Machine for that either. Whatever the Contagion ends up being might be what I'll go with.<br /> <br /> (granted this is a bit of a massive undertaking to juggle that many Eras and gamelines so haven't exactly attempted to actually do this yet. So who knows)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T20:33:58-07:00","id":1131587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1131570#post1131570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean, like, a metaplot?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not at all like a metaplot. I lived through oWoD, I loved the grand experiment of it and, no, I don't want CoD to go down the same road. And, actually, what I want is irrelevant. CoD isn't built to support that.<br /> <br /> I mean like a self contained story wrapped into an event format. Imagine if Fall of Camarilla wasn't an adventure book but an ongoing thing with online support, etc. Or, better yet, if Orpheus was something like that. You get a core book with a bunch of material to use. Then, ongoing developments re published digitally. You're free to ignore them or use them however the heck you want, but if you choose to follow them, perhaps there's a way to register your group and submit the outcomes for each of the chapters, that might influence the way things develop. An IC-only subforum, some light official moderation, etc. You know, a way to get everyone excited and engaged. It wraps up after a while and it doesn't need to be canon after the fact. Just a cool community event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T20:44:08-07:00","id":1131589,"title":"","content":"I figure the extra books would go into specific details that wouldn't be necessary for the 'core'. So further details, like how everyone's dream abilities interact, or what happens with micro-templates, like ghoul proximi, or when such things gain their main template, if a proximus who becomes a Beast turns out different.<br /> <br /> The Contagion itself seems like a shard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T20:48:50-07:00","id":1131591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dawngreeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1131587#post1131587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, not at all like a metaplot. I lived through oWoD, I loved the grand experiment of it and, no, I don't want CoD to go down the same road. And, actually, what I want is irrelevant. CoD isn't built to support that.<br /> <br /> I mean like a self contained story wrapped into an event format. Imagine if Fall of Camarilla wasn't an adventure book but an ongoing thing with online support, etc. Or, better yet, if Orpheus was something like that. You get a core book with a bunch of material to use. Then, ongoing developments re published digitally. You're free to ignore them or use them however the heck you want, but if you choose to follow them, perhaps there's a way to register your group and submit the outcomes for each of the chapters, that might influence the way things develop. An IC-only subforum, some light official moderation, etc. You know, a way to get everyone excited and engaged. It wraps up after a while and it doesn't need to be canon after the fact. Just a cool community event.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, still sounds like metaplot to me, just one clearly signposted as optional. Maybe I'm just misunderstanding you, or maybe we have different ideas of what the word metaplot means. At any rate, personally what you're suggesting doesn't sound appealing to me. But I am interested in the idea of this book, even if it's not what I was expecting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T22:56:02-07:00","id":1131630,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping it gives good advice on how to give every splat a moment to shine and a moment to realize why they are working with all these other weirdos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T23:13:09-07:00","id":1131634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1131630#post1131630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping it gives good advice on how to give every splat a moment to shine and a moment to realize why they are working with all these other weirdos.</div> </div> </div> </div>It will, and those won't be restricted to the Contagion, though as the title implies, it is at the core of historic reasons the creatures from the game lines have had cause to unite.<br /> <br /> I am enjoying the speculation. More information will be released soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:21:00-07:00","id":1131796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1131591#post1131591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, still sounds like metaplot to me, just one clearly signposted as optional. Maybe I'm just misunderstanding you, or maybe we have different ideas of what the word metaplot means. At any rate, personally what you're suggesting doesn't sound appealing to me. But I am interested in the idea of this book, even if it's not what I was expecting.</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition (or at least mine) a metaplot is not optional, and advances the setting overall. The Contagion outbreaks, from the sound of it, are not those-unless there is a date for an outbreak that will happen, it is simply an obscure danger. Don't want to use it, it just doesn't infect any local areas and what outbreaks do happen are relatively minor rather than cataclysms.<br /> <br /> Me, I'm hoping for strains of the Contagion, to emphasize it is, in fact, an eldritch organism, an anti-God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:50:34-07:00","id":1131814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1131796#post1131796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By definition (or at least mine) a metaplot is not optional, and advances the setting overall. The Contagion outbreaks, from the sound of it, are not those-unless there is a date for an outbreak that will happen, it is simply an obscure danger. Don't want to use it, it just doesn't infect any local areas and what outbreaks do happen are relatively minor rather than cataclysms.<br /> <br /> Me, I'm hoping for strains of the Contagion, to emphasize it is, in fact, an eldritch organism, an anti-God-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing I disagree with is metaplot being non-optional (really, nothing in an RPG is truly non-optional). I agree that the outbreaks are sounding like historical events in the setting, not like metaplot events. I was referring specifically to Dawngreeter's suggestion of an ongoing story with events that develop over time based on player-submitted outcomes to previous story events. That's like... Exactly what a metaplot is - ongoing story events that have an impact on the setting post-year 0. Fortunately (in my opinion) that doesn't sound to me like what the Contagion Chronicle is going to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T12:11:41-07:00","id":1131824,"title":"","content":"well, while the Contagion has a scent of metaplot to it, considering how most Chronicle books work, I really don't think it is going to be the case. It would be metaplot if suddenly a new outbreak of an unknown virus would force the different supernatural critters of the setting to band together against a common enemy, but as Matthew said, it is not something new, but an historic reason. The Contagion is not new- it is old, perhaps as humanity. It infect the strix, twists the idigam and make the Insatiable to go mad. Metaplot is only valid for new and sudden changes to the setting- not retroactive additions to it. Else, every time we get a new gameline it would be considered as &quot;Metaplot&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T12:19:43-07:00","id":1131832,"title":"","content":"More of a metaplot if it changes existing things, using a 'plot' as the reason for it. For instance if the Plague Angel created a Contagion, and thats why vampires are different between first and second editions.<br /> <br /> New books, and this Contagion thing, seem to be shedding light on existing things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T16:34:39-07:00","id":1131943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1131634#post1131634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It will, and those won't be restricted to the Contagion, though as the title implies, it is at the core of historic reasons the creatures from the game lines have had cause to unite.<br /> <br /> I am enjoying the speculation. More information will be released soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>So maybe Contigan is less of a Shard (except for the most extreme outbreak maybe), but just something that has out breaks every once in a while through history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T20:38:13-07:00","id":1132033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1131634#post1131634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It will, and those won't be restricted to the Contagion, though as the title implies, it is at the core of historic reasons the creatures from the game lines have had cause to unite.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds very much as <b>Dark Eras</b> take, to be frank. Much more 'Points of Light historical settings' ( from D&amp;D terminology ) than WoD Metaplot model.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-21-2017, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T22:37:21-07:00","id":1132086,"title":"","content":"This is interesting, but I'm curious to see how it plays out.<br /> <br /> It's interesting that they're giving it an &quot;X Chronicles&quot; title, since that follows the model for the standalone lines. My presumption is that, like the Strix or God-Machine or Slashers or whomever, Contagion will represent some sort of existential danger that ties into the book's theme, without superimposing those threats onto the other game lines. So I guess the question is, what sort of overarching theme makes sense for all of the splats (or whichever splats they include, rather. Perhaps this isn't a full-bore crossover?).<br /> <br /> I'd guess, since it's supposed to be a crossover game, it's not going to be standalone in the same way as the 2e cores, but is it possible it could be? A core book that uses a variation of Dread Powers for character building, some specific crunch for monster-on-monster interaction, and simplified versions of the core monsters as splat templates? If the Contagion mutates the various supernaturals, that could provide good reason to get creative with the mixing and matching of power sets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T12:27:15-07:00","id":1133112,"title":"","content":"Today I realised what this reminded me of: Three Shades of Night. In that book too you had multiple supernaturals (vampires, werewolves, mages) dealing with a grave, near-cataclysmic situation together and a major part of it was a supernatural contagion. I wonder if the Contagion chronicles will reference this somehow and whether it was what brought up the initial idea for the Contagion Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T17:08:22-07:00","id":1133216,"title":"","content":"Given that the God Machine Chronicles was born from one short piece of fiction in the first edition core...I would say the odds are good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T19:44:41-07:00","id":1133262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1133112#post1133112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today I realised what this reminded me of: Three Shades of Night. In that book too you had multiple supernaturals (vampires, werewolves, mages) dealing with a grave, near-cataclysmic situation together and a major part of it was a supernatural contagion. I wonder if the Contagion chronicles will reference this somehow and whether it was what brought up the initial idea for the Contagion Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was the first World of Darkness/Chronicles of Darkness fiction I ever bought. Loved it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T19:59:07-07:00","id":1133265,"title":"","content":"Have some more info on Contagion from <b>Three Shades of Night</b>? Did not read, but maybe something was spilled then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T00:52:22-07:00","id":1133297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1133265#post1133265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have some more info on Contagion from <b>Three Shades of Night</b>? Did not read, but maybe something was spilled then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoilers for <i>Three Shades of Night</i> following:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The contagion in the book was the &quot;muskegon virus&quot; (which seems to be fictional) that was mainly transmitted by mosquitos, crows and ... vampires. Within the fiction, the regular version of the muskegon virus mostly affected the young and elderly but the big contagion they are fighting was supernaturally amplified, leading to almost certain death no matter the physical fitness of whoever caught it. I am a bit hazy on the details, but I think the cause for how the muskegon virus got out of hand was the shitty spiritual landscape of Chicago (might be a Wound there somewhere?), which also led to many catastrophic accidents and other weirdness. In the past, this was in fact the cause for the Great Chicago Fire, which the Big Three back in that day could not prevent because a vampire flaked out on being a sacrifice for a Cr\u00faac rite meant to fix the situation. In the book they managed to prevent a second major catastrophe coming to the city, the Cronies actually could go through with the rite this time, easing the overall situation, while the werewolves and mages battled the sick spirit that was the cause of it.<br /> <br /> So as far as participation goes, the vampires are the first to notice something is awry because of it affecting them first and they provided the Cr\u00faac rite. Werewolves had the spirit expertise to figure out what was the base cause of all the shit that was happening and the Awakened were there to put all the disparate supernatural elements together.<br /> <br /> Also the Unholy shows up at one point.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It is unlikely that this particular contagion is the one talked about in the brochure, but it seems possible that the general idea was inspired by the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T11:46:33-07:00","id":1134203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1131085#post1131085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have to say, it's sounding less and less like the book I wanted the more I hear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, sadly. There is one slant that might make it better: if it's not a threat so blatant as to force all the supes to work together, but rather a threat so <i>subtle</i> that only supes who are working together and combining their perspectives can see it. I can't really fault coming up with an X-chronicle thing that applies equally to everyone - that's how the second edition books are structured - but I'd rather it had a similar role to the Strix in Blood and Smoke, a good hostis genera when you need one, but with enough material it never has to come into play as more than a rumour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T12:11:51-07:00","id":1134212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1134203#post1134203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but I'd rather it had a similar role to the Strix in Blood and Smoke, a good hostis genera when you need one, but with enough material it never has to come into play as more than a rumour.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see any reason to assume the eponymous Contagion won't fill that role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T13:47:07-07:00","id":1134243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1134212#post1134212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any reason to assume the eponymous Contagion won't fill that role.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much hope it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T22:45:08-07:00","id":1134360,"title":"","content":"My predictions:<br /> \u200b1-Local breakouts and flare ups, keeping it personal and intimate, as opposed to a global epidemic that demands global attention.<br /> \u200b2-It will effect each splat and their little world differently, possibly attacking things like Ghouls, Wolf-Blooded and other connected mini templates instead of the splats directly.<br /> \u200b3-Either each manifestation will be immune or highly resistant to the powers of the splat to which it was tailored, or each splat will be able to stamp down their own strain but as long as any of the strains are still active in the area all of them will flare up again. Either way the different splats will be best served by coordinating their efforts in order to clear the contagion from their region, at least until the next outsider brings it back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T23:49:32-07:00","id":1135081,"title":"","content":"Man, it's like, for 2018 Chronicles it's like they looked at my desk and went &quot;what books is raygun REALLY gonna want?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T09:28:09-07:00","id":1135178,"title":"","content":"I'm very excited for this","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T10:12:02-07:00","id":1135193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1130466#post1130466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how I feel about the Contagion thing, partly because I don't know what to expect from it and partly because I was hoping this book would primarily be mechanical and thematic advice for blending the lines. Pinning the book on an external threat makes me worry a little bit about how much actual crossover we'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that the Contagion thing will be about as important as, say, the Strix in V2e: it's there as a ready-made set of hooks to facilitate crossover play, but it is in no way mandated as the only way that crossover play can be done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T10:59:19-07:00","id":1135206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1135193#post1135193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect that the Contagion thing will be about as important as, say, the Strix in V2e: it's there as a ready-made set of hooks to facilitate crossover play, but it is in no way mandated as the only way that crossover play can be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully it won't become a point of proselytization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T11:06:06-07:00","id":1135209,"title":"","content":"I see the future now. Dozens of posts. 'I don't like the Contagion Chronicle because I don't like metaplot,' in every sub-forum, used to start entirely unrelated topics or interrupt others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T11:18:50-07:00","id":1135214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1135209#post1135209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see the future now. Dozens of posts. 'I don't like the Contagion Chronicle because I don't like metaplot,' in every sub-forum, used to start entirely unrelated topics or interrupt others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely, what with people treating the example domains and hunting ground as Word of God instead of plot hooks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T11:25:16-07:00","id":1135215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1135193#post1135193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect that the Contagion thing will be about as important as, say, the Strix in V2e: it's there as a ready-made set of hooks to facilitate crossover play, but it is in no way mandated as the only way that crossover play can be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ding ding ding. <br /> <br /> We are not introducing metaplot into the Chronicles of Darkness. <br /> <br /> Will the Contagion be referenced obliquely in other books? Possibly, if you're looking for it. <br /> <br /> Will it change any Chronicles of Darkness line, requiring you to own this book to understand said changes? By the God-Machine, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T14:01:16-07:00","id":1135264,"title":"","content":"I know, it's just people take these things the wrong way. They're still calling the God-Machine and strix metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T14:26:23-07:00","id":1135267,"title":"","content":"Many gamers believe the phrase &quot;caveat emptor&quot; is lazy, but the whole Chronicles of Darkness line is full of options to include or remove. If I ran a chronicle of Requiem with every bloodline, Discipline, and sub-faction of each covenant present, it would be a mess. You pick and choose.<br /> <br /> I've said it before, but my design style if utility. I prefer to give players and Storytellers options and gripping chronicle hooks over hard-and-fast rules for play. If I write a Discipline, I want every level of that Discipline to have a story behind it. One night there may come a coterie who wish to study the genesis of Dominate, and behold, each level offers a tease about the first recorded user, or one of its most famed implementations, or the way certain vampires use it. The same goes with the Contagion. Every paragraph must give options, story hooks, or simply spark imagination. I want to make chronicles ever more exciting and fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T14:32:00-07:00","id":1135269,"title":"","content":"How dare you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T15:23:21-07:00","id":1135277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1133297#post1133297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spoilers for <i>Three Shades of Night</i> following:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The contagion in the book was the &quot;muskegon virus&quot; (which seems to be fictional) that was mainly transmitted by mosquitos, crows and ... vampires. Within the fiction, the regular version of the muskegon virus mostly affected the young and elderly but the big contagion they are fighting was supernaturally amplified, leading to almost certain death no matter the physical fitness of whoever caught it. I am a bit hazy on the details, but I think the cause for how the muskegon virus got out of hand was the shitty spiritual landscape of Chicago (might be a Wound there somewhere?), which also led to many catastrophic accidents and other weirdness. In the past, this was in fact the cause for the Great Chicago Fire, which the Big Three back in that day could not prevent because a vampire flaked out on being a sacrifice for a Cr\u00faac rite meant to fix the situation. In the book they managed to prevent a second major catastrophe coming to the city, the Cronies actually could go through with the rite this time, easing the overall situation, while the werewolves and mages battled the sick spirit that was the cause of it.<br /> <br /> So as far as participation goes, the vampires are the first to notice something is awry because of it affecting them first and they provided the Cr\u00faac rite. Werewolves had the spirit expertise to figure out what was the base cause of all the shit that was happening and the Awakened were there to put all the disparate supernatural elements together.<br /> <br /> Also the Unholy shows up at one point.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It is unlikely that this particular contagion is the one talked about in the brochure, but it seems possible that the general idea was inspired by the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loved that book ^.^. It's what made the Unholy so interesting to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T08:06:55-07:00","id":1135453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1135215#post1135215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are not introducing metaplot into the Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Metaplot doesn't seem to be what Dataweaver (or Lex) was talking about there, but that aside, if &quot;Contagion is about as prevalent as the Strix&quot; is correct, that's good news in my book. My worry was that it would be more prominent, not in a metaplot way, but in a giving-short-shrift-to-crossover-in-general way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T08:47:25-07:00","id":1135461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1135453#post1135453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My worry was that it would be more prominent, not in a metaplot way, but in a giving-short-shrift-to-crossover-in-general way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heavily doubt they would even bother with such a project if that was it's aim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T10:42:55-07:00","id":1135499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1135453#post1135453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metaplot doesn't seem to be what Dataweaver (or Lex) was talking about there, but that aside, if &amp;quot;Contagion is about as prevalent as the Strix&amp;quot; is correct, that's good news in my book. My worry was that it would be more prominent, not in a metaplot way, but in a giving-short-shrift-to-crossover-in-general way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was the one who brought up metaplot, and it was in response to another user's suggestion of what they hoped CC might be like, not to what I thought CC would actually be like. I too like the sound of the Contagion being to CC as the Strix are to Requiem 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T10:49:49-07:00","id":1135504,"title":"","content":"More info to run Mummy/X crossovers? I'll take it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T11:54:28-07:00","id":1135525,"title":"","content":"So, what would make the Contagion something that tends to facilitate crossover play? One theory: we've been told that the Contagion infects each gameline's antagonists, presumably enhancing them in some way. You might get super-strix or super-Pandorans or super-goblins, etc. (where, by \u201csuper\u201d, I mean \u201charder for the gameline's protagonists to deal with). But what if this comes coupled with a general vulnerability to the other gamelines? <br /> <br /> These enhanced Hosts might be nightmares for the Uratha to deal with; but the Kindred are able to discover a fairly straightforward way to put them down. Conversely, the Contagion-infected Strix might make the Kindreds' Unlives even more of a living hell than usual; but the Uratha can tear them to shreds without too much trouble. So an alliance between vampires and werewolves would be able to deal with the Contagion far more effectively than either one on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T12:52:28-07:00","id":1135558,"title":"","content":"Following the significance of what contagion means could also point to a sort of blurring between the antagonist. We could be seeing something like a strix host or an abyssal idigam or an ... hero(ic) angel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T13:06:43-07:00","id":1135563,"title":"","content":"The Contagion as an exploration in the ChroD of the concept of the Abomination? Hmm\u2026 if handled with care, this could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T13:09:52-07:00","id":1135564,"title":"","content":"It could also be different realms spilling into another, hence the need to interact with those who populate each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T13:23:51-07:00","id":1135569,"title":"","content":"That could work for those gamelines that feature other realms. But last I checked, Vampire, Promethean, and Demon don't feature any \u201cotherworlds\u201d per se, and would be left out of that was all that gets featured. (And while Mummy technically has something like this, the Death Cycle seems to be more like a personal dreamscape than a realm.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T13:34:57-07:00","id":1135576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1135569#post1135569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could work for those gamelines that feature other realms. But last I checked, Vampire, Promethean, and Demon don't feature any \u201cotherworlds\u201d per se, and would be left out of that was all that gets featured. (And while Mummy technically has something like this, the Death Cycle seems to be more like a personal dreamscape than a realm.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean deal with the rivers of the dead, and the shadow on a lesser scale, and Demons could deal with assignments virtually anywhere. I've nothing on Mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T13:57:19-07:00","id":1135585,"title":"","content":"The Death Cycle is to Mummy as the Underworld Rivers are to Promethean: it's where the Arisen go when they die while still on their Descent. <br /> <br /> The Underworld Rivers aren't really a Promethean thing; they're more of a Sin-Eater thing that Prometheans have a (limited) relationship with. And the Shadow has even less to do with Prometheans than the Underworld does. <br /> <br /> That said, this is one of those things that I'm expecting Contagion Chronicles to address: what the various otherworlds are, and how each gameline relates to them. That said, I'll be surprised if the Contagion gets hard-linked to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T14:23:31-07:00","id":1135597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1135585#post1135585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, this is one of those things that I'm expecting Contagion Chronicles to address: what the various otherworlds are, and how each gameline relates to them. That said, I'll be surprised if the Contagion gets hard-linked to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage has an upcoming book on that.<br /> <br /> Some Prometheans are made of spirits, so you do have some Shadow-stuff there, they've got as much to do with it as they do the Underworld, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T14:24:42-07:00","id":1135599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1135569#post1135569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could work for those gamelines that feature other realms. But last I checked, Vampire, Promethean, and Demon don't feature any \u201cotherworlds\u201d per se, and would be left out of that was all that gets featured. (And while Mummy technically has something like this, the Death Cycle seems to be more like a personal dreamscape than a realm.)</div> </div> </div> </div>All those mingling realms could also be invading the physical world, which would definitely be an issue for all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T09:39:47-07:00","id":1137719,"title":"","content":"What if this Contagion is a Abyssal thing? Wouldn't the mages be all over that like white on rice? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T10:02:35-07:00","id":1137730,"title":"","content":"Eh. Mages don't need a reason to be all over the Contagion like white on rice: the Contagion, whatever it is, is almost certainly a Mystery and a source of Mysteries. And as we all know, mages are Addicted to Mysteries. <br /> <br /> And I don't want everything infected by the Contagion to stink of the Abyss. So it's best that they be separate things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T06:47:44-07:00","id":1138308,"title":"","content":"Edit: Nevermind, Dataweaver said it better and pointed to things I hadn't considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T11:53:54-07:00","id":1138954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1137730#post1137730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don't want everything infected by the Contagion to stink of the Abyss. So it's best that they be separate things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figure it's more likely to be a Lower Depth of some kind - while that's a <i>term</i> mages use, the <i>concept</i> it refers to is Chrodwide.<br /> <br /> The other thing that occurs to me is that it might originate strictly from within humanity, since all the species have to orbit humanity in some way. Maybe a mutation of the human soul that does something to supernaturals who come into contact with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T19:34:12-08:00","id":1166889,"title":"","content":"So, looks like the Contagion Chronicle has officially entered the MMN and is in the first draft stage!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T22:28:54-08:00","id":1166914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book?p=1166889#post1166889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, looks like the Contagion Chronicle has officially entered the MMN and is in the first draft stage!</div> </div> </div> </div>I was surprised to see that. I honestly thought they would hold out for confirmation on MtC 2nd Ed first, just so they include them. The 1.5 edition stuff is a complaint I've seen about the changeling dark eras, (phrased as 'can you please update x?').","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T22:59:29-08:00","id":1166918,"title":"","content":"It could be that the MtC 2E team is working underwraps as the Geist 2E team did. And with the Contagion Chronicle being a crossover gameline, it may take longer to edit and draw all those pieces together than the usual CoD gameline, giving MtC 2E a change to pop up before CC leaves 1st draft time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T08:03:56-08:00","id":1167002,"title":"","content":"I think they already confirmed Mummy second edition.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yes, it was in the brochure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-12-2017, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactio